---
# XmegaTimer's code from before the template, until a later version rewrites it in the namespace
# xmega_timer (OIL 4): its names, macros, typedefs and C enums are what these groups report, and
# its bitwise operators on registers and initializations with = are what the template's
# house-bitwise-in-bit-class and house-braced-var-init of v0.8.0 report (CodingStyle H-9, T-3).
# They come on with that version, each with what it finds fixed, and this file goes then. The
# tests and the mock are new and keep every check, as do the headers of src/xmega_timer/, which
# the tests include.
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: >
  -bugprone-assignment-in-if-condition,
  -bugprone-signed-bitwise,
  -house-bitwise-in-bit-class,
  -house-braced-var-init,
  -cppcoreguidelines-*,
  -google-*,
  -misc-*,
  -modernize-*,
  -performance-enum-size,
  -readability-*
